# R2.1 — Seven product wholes and the six-product section

**Standing:** substantive R1 release and R2 development, with a separate same-runtime semantic revision pass. This is not the independent R5 review, completion of R3/R4, T25 closure or Frank's T26 ratification. Canonical execution continues from `main@13b43fe290ee3dbc1d6686709f2e7bc4e7158292`. The local Git commit is a diff base reproducing its canonical files, not a substitute remote base and never a commit to push.

## Governing return

The [R1 grounding return](R1-GROUNDING-RETURN.md) closes the plan-first opening and releases S development. It recovers the complete native I–XI theorem, A/C ruling and primitive constitution, the relevant Subject/means/World dependencies, and the precise Indian zero-denominator scene in the retained Kaplan and Colebrooke routes. The intended Abhinavagupta interval remains an exact source-collation debt. No new general authorial approval is required. Deeper supporting-file and transverse-carrier reads belong to the full-field continuation and are not counted as complete merely because their routes were identified.

S now develops World and Life, keeping Objective Internality's mediating office within the whole Life/Mind relation. Six substantive product bodies and their locally developed sixfolds make the accepted meanings operative. The actual shared field is 144 distinct records: 36 A, 36 A′, 64 C, A/C and seven S. The prior 281-record admitted census is preserved; a separate seven-record refinement admission gives 288 currently admitted publication records. Neither number counts every page, source or register object. T26 acceptance is not inferred from admission.

