## Source and implementation standing

The three accepted September inputs are retained untouched and housed as one recoverable authorial dialogue commission. Its SOURCE has `dialogue_role: provenance-of-thinking` and `evidence_status: never-evidence`; it carries no citation/quotation readiness fields. It licenses the authored product meanings, not external historical claims or implementation success. The June twelve-lens source and its protected authorial originals remain intact; its dated difference from the adopted September Scientific sequence is explicit.

The Indian/Kashmiri connection remains substantive: the selected Bhāskara II zero-denominator/divine-invariance scene is distinguished from earlier placeholders, arithmetic rules and first-invention claims. The precise Abhinavagupta interval and edition/Sanskrit collation remain named, limited tasks. Gebser and ordinary/extraordinary reports remain positive psychic-fact relations rather than exclusion tests. No sixth Gebser structure is invented for the authored supramental extension.

The O:I constructor/source snapshot is retained at its actual dated standing. No product-repository code was changed or freshly certified in this essay lane. New comparisons are Offered experiments with conditions, contrary outcomes and a returned difference to test. Argued philosophical meanings are not weakened because those experiments remain unrun. The general all-lens CSV overlay remains a separately recorded follow-on.

## Separate revision pass and corrections

Reviewer: the same GPT execution runtime, in a second content-reading pass against the accepted minute, full retained pair reading, native field and G1–G10/comparative-negation gate. This is explicitly not an independent reviewer/model and not R5 certification. All seven new S bodies and the six new movement bodies were reread; the entire Homeric net and Indra-net wholes were reopened. Full prior technical bodies were checked against the transport manifest, not a word-count approximation. No calibration exemplars or installed S5 prose skill were loaded.

The pass corrected actual sentences and relations: the initially over-strong measurable-O:I opening in the transported J-Space passage; a moved link that had broken “hidden determining measure”; native Workcell and QL primitive names recovered from A/C rather than plausible replacements; BOTH narrowed to a permission-scope example; dated literature-search language; and the bare argmax index's piecewise-constant/discontinuous operation distinguished from training with a probability loss. The unchanged productive offices of distinction, refusal, joining and renewal remain positive. The review does not use a token match for “dia” or “syn” as proof of comprehension.

Retained distinctions pass the comparison gate for a specified reason: whole versus technical instance prevents a change of subject; source versus inferred claim preserves attribution; Gate versus Recognition preserves separate evidence; availability versus permission preserves another's answer; historical witness versus native theorem preserves derivational authorship. Generic caveats are not counted as depth. Canonical movement planning still names its operational/source limits; manuscript prose remains for the post-T26 writing pass.

## Executed validation and precise limits

- The first full local run executed 124 tests: five failures and one unavailable-AIKit skip. Its failures exposed stale model-owner expectations, unrecognised block-form P1 alignment, the newly admitted product domain and the new commission source count. These were repaired rather than hidden by dropping the assertions.
- The second full local run executed 125 tests in 383.925 seconds: one remaining stale `j-space` assertion failed, with the same one AIKit skip. The correct current model-field consumer is C40. After that assertion was corrected, the actual context regression passed independently in 7.854 seconds, retaining A14, source, predecessor/successor and product-trace requirements.
- The eight product-field regressions passed against the actual repository: identities, parent/member/types/register, both full pairs, movement order, source houses, provenance boundary, navigation and all six transported technical bodies. The seven current pre-manuscript gate tests also passed after block-route and refinement-admission repair.
- All three real builders and their `--check` commands passed. The default room-depth audit now tests all eight declared rooms while keeping the historical `arguments/` shelf distinct; missing or unknown actual room directories remain failures. The real default audit returned eight passes.
- Reader/pre-manuscript reports show 144 shared identities and 288 admitted records, with no missing or duplicate identities/homes, no missing 48-movement alignment or next link, and no lost reader route among the 556 saved routes checked. The audit's earlier #5 lookup typo for the S return was corrected to the actual #5→0 heads. A report-generation exit code is not semantic acceptance.
- The 410 saved paragraph witnesses have 294 exact and 92 same-text-after-link-normalisation matches; 24 changed witnesses remain for explicit R3/R5 review. The six moved technical bodies have separate exact operation-preservation witnesses here. Those facts do not clear the full historical review by implication.
- Every one of the 472 starting protected-file hashes matches. A/C's complete prefix through the ethical and primitive constitution, before `The shared close`, is byte-equivalent to the admitted R1.2 base. Raw originals, NOTES, private Control references and sovereign manuscript are untouched. `git diff --check` passes.

The hash-pinned admission must rerun the **complete** suite and all builders/checks on the exact staged canonical payload before it can fast-forward main. Its separately generated `R2-ADMISSION-VALIDATION.json` records the real command result and validated payload; until that record exists, this receipt does not call the final whole suite green.

